{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/settings/screens.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-10T22:00:22.643292Z","id":"c5ae0cdee9ad4315288dae95f408ff3ed0f241bfbbc3e317785a03a4bacdf890","body":{"detail":"SCREENS' items are written by hand from each screen's headings and controls. web/shell/src/settings/screens.test.ts (\"are IDs the screens' sources carry\") fails when an item's `#<ID>` is no heading's ID in people/, hosted/, bot/ or q/, but nothing fails when a screen gains a section or a control and no item names it, or when a heading's text changes and the item's title does not. Configuration's fields come from GET /api/settings and are indexed only by table ([serve], [bot], ...), not by field.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":46},"end":{"line":184},"content_hash":"12611badadff006ed04d21344740c65db41c789bc30d3e26483d473fea832c3b"},"summary":"Settings' search finds only what this hand-kept list names: a control added to a screen is not found until an item is added for it","tags":["session:claude-code:eada89d1-d2ee-4104-9ad9-445efa856fbf"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/settings/context.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-10T22:00:22.643354Z","id":"dd343a253338688bf29a9810457593494e5427efa9b6f7aca957af863618c90d","body":{"detail":"context() keeps its first answer for the page's life. When the owner revokes a person whose Settings is open, the screen shown says so (web/shell/src/people/People.svelte, `denied`) and the header's gear goes (MemberLinks, on clax:people-gone), but Settings' navigation and the search dialog still list that person's screens until the page loads again; the same holds for a member made an admin, or ClaxBot turned on. Each screen's own requests are still refused by the daemon, so nothing is shown that the person may not see.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":7},"end":{"line":31},"content_hash":"74b0107ff2b3facb2591cd910dfcd81dcd927263d7445f4427835da6dc77e6ab"},"summary":"Settings asks who the browser is once per page, so a change of role or membership shows in its navigation and search only after a reload","tags":["session:claude-code:eada89d1-d2ee-4104-9ad9-445efa856fbf"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/settings/screens.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-10T22:00:22.643377Z","id":"39883d9165e2ed69967cdfc03c1d3e81621e3e61c007f68bad8c1e279eb314a2","body":{"detail":"They stay on /queues and /tags, and Settings' search lists them under Elsewhere, opening those pages. Not taken: a queue's Manage panel is part of the Queues page a member triages from (web/shell/src/queues/Queues.svelte, QueueAdmin.svelte), per queue, and Tags is reached from the gallery's tag bar; moving either splits a page people work in.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":172},"end":{"line":183},"content_hash":"6eb857210225bde422af89799053c5c2fc5437ddc9aade396c4d1d39d2bf0236"},"summary":"Move a queue's management (members, service grants) and the Tags page into Settings as screens","tags":["revisit:queue management is separated from triage, or people look for tags under Settings","session:claude-code:eada89d1-d2ee-4104-9ad9-445efa856fbf"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/settings/palette.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-10T22:00:22.643400Z","id":"4289842d4bcbf25796866cfb3ed8601fcbd5dc5206ba6e7cc0f049c4626920b3","body":{"detail":"openPalette imports Palette.svelte and asks context() before it mounts the dialog; until then the focus is wherever it was. web/e2e/settings.spec.ts waits for the field to have the focus before typing for this reason. Loading the chunk when the gear mounts (people/MemberLinks.svelte) would close the gap at the cost of one more request on every gallery page.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":22},"end":{"line":29},"content_hash":"2caa2eaa543217b980e95ae3d1c0b629f6a507b5e02c476450bb431c0c302e7b"},"summary":"Keys typed right after the Settings key, before the search dialog's chunk has loaded for the first time on a page, go to the page instead of the search field","tags":["session:claude-code:eada89d1-d2ee-4104-9ad9-445efa856fbf"]}}
